<!--META-DATA
{
	tags: logical, min,
}
-->

<statement>
<p>
	This function determines whether an undirected graph is simple . A graph is considered simple if it has no self-loops (edges that connect a vertex to itself) and no multiple edges (more than one edge between any pair of vertices).
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Inputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>G</pf> (struct) number — : A structure representing the graph containing, at minimum, the following fields:</p>
			<p><pf>G.adj_mat</pf> (n x n) number — : The adjacency matrix of the graph.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Outputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>result</pf> (logical) logical — : Returns true if the graph is simple, false otherwise.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>This program is relatively easy. The key is to use the adjacency matrix to detect loops or parallel edges in the graph.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>Command Window Expected Output G.adj_mat = [0 1 0; 1 0 1; 0 1 0]; result = HW5P4_is_simple(G); result = logical 1 G.adj_mat = [1 1 0; 1 0 1; 0 1 0]; result = HW5P4_is_simple(G); result = logical 0 G.adj_mat = [0 2 0; 2 0 1; 0 1 0]; result = HW5P4_is_simple(G); result = logical 0 G.adj_mat = [0 0 0; 0 0 0; 0 0 0]; result = HW5P4_is_simple(G); result = logical 1</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>Expected Output</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>result = logical 1</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>result = logical 0</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>result = logical 0</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>result = logical 1</p></cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

</statement>
